From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:16:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: log a guest split lock's exception once in 65536, not
 each time

prepare_exception_arm64ec printed its "[rtcs] pre" line for every
exception: the brace of its 40-line cap closes before the line. A
misaligned atomic (a guest split lock, an x86 lock xadd or xchg on a
slot that crosses a 16-byte boundary, which FEX completes) comes
through here once per execution. Jurassic World Evolution's protected
code runs about 14,000 a second (496,416 lines in a 44 s run), and the
split-lock probe measures 61 to 75 us an operation on the phone.

Misalignments are now counted, and the first 8 and every 65536th are
logged with the count. Every other exception code is logged as before.

Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-12-guest-split-locks.md
Offered-upstream: no; the line is the iOS port's
---
 dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
index ca8b951..fdf97d9 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
@@ -3924,6 +3924,22 @@ static void * __attribute__((used)) prepare_exception_arm64ec( EXCEPTION_RECORD
                     }
                 }
             }
+        /* PLA-242: a misaligned atomic (a guest split lock, which FEX completes)
+         * comes through here once per execution, hundreds of thousands of times
+         * in a protected game: count those, and log the first 8 and every
+         * 65536th with the count. Every other code is logged as before. */
+        if (rec->ExceptionCode == STATUS_DATATYPE_MISALIGNMENT)
+        {
+            static LONG misalign_n;
+            LONG n = InterlockedIncrement( &misalign_n );
+            if (n <= 8 || !(n % 65536))
+                ERR( "[rtcs] pre: code=%08x addr=%p armPc=%p ecRip=%p rtcs=%p insim=%u (misaligned #%ld; "
+                     "the first 8 and every 65536th are logged)\n",
+                     (unsigned int)rec->ExceptionCode, rec->ExceptionAddress,
+                     (void *)(ULONG_PTR)arm_ctx->Pc, (void *)(ULONG_PTR)context->AMD64_Context.Rip,
+                     pResetToConsistentState, get_arm64ec_cpu_area()->InSimulation, n );
+        }
+        else
             ERR( "[rtcs] pre: code=%08x addr=%p armPc=%p ecRip=%p rtcs=%p insim=%u\n",
                  (unsigned int)rec->ExceptionCode, rec->ExceptionAddress,
                  (void *)(ULONG_PTR)arm_ctx->Pc, (void *)(ULONG_PTR)context->AMD64_Context.Rip,
